   "text": {
    "L1": "A government makes rules and decisions for everyone. It also keeps order, settles disputes, and provides services such as schools and roads.",
    "L2": "Different governments place power in different hands. A monarchy gives the position to a king or queen by birth.",
    "L3": "In an absolute monarchy, the ruler has almost all power. In a constitutional monarchy, elected representatives make laws and limit the monarch's powers.",
    "L4": "In a democracy, power comes from the people. Citizens may vote directly, or elect representatives to decide for them.",
    "L5": "A dictatorship keeps power with one person or a small group, often by force. A theocracy is ruled by religious leaders, while an oligarchy is ruled by a small group.",
    "L6": "Voting is not enough for democracy. It also needs equal rights, free speech, a free press, the rule of law, and courts that can check leaders."
   },
   "narration": {
